stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    %% The displayed labels make the owning Replica's role explicit while the
    %% aliases keep the actual FSM state names available to Mermaid.
    state "WATCHING<br/>(follower Replica)" as WATCHING
    state "COORDINATOR<br/>(coordinator Replica)" as COORDINATOR

    %% This diagram models one HeartbeatTransaction owned by one Replica.
    %% It handles repeated heartbeat periods for one coordinator term and ends
    %% when its owner crashes or responsibility passes to ElectionTransaction.

    %% [*] as a source represents the beginning of the transaction lifecycle.
    [*] --> STOPPED: transaction created

    %% After InitSystem, the owner compares its ID with the coordinator ID and
    %% starts the transaction in the role appropriate for this coordinator term.
    STOPPED --> COORDINATOR: start as coordinator Replica
    STOPPED --> WATCHING: start as follower Replica

    %% HeartbeatTick is an internal message sent by the Akka Scheduler to the
    %% coordinator Replica's mailbox. Handling it broadcasts HEARTBEAT and
    %% schedules the next one-shot HeartbeatTick.
    COORDINATOR --> COORDINATOR: HeartbeatTick / broadcast HEARTBEAT and schedule next tick

    %% If the owner itself crashes, it cannot perform another transition or send
    %% a cleanup message. This local HeartbeatTransaction simply stops running.
    COORDINATOR --> [*]: coordinator Replica crashes

    %% A valid network HEARTBEAT comes from the coordinator monitored by this
    %% transaction. It keeps the follower in WATCHING and restarts its watchdog.
    WATCHING --> WATCHING: valid HEARTBEAT / cancel and restart watchdog

    %% WatchdogExpired is an internal scheduler message. The watchdog version in
    %% the message must match the currently active version; stale timeouts caused
    %% by earlier, cancelled watchdogs are ignored without changing state.
    WATCHING --> ELECTION_REQUESTED: active WatchdogExpired / request ElectionTransaction

    %% This state records that the follower has detected the coordinator failure
    %% and requested exactly one election. Further timeout events are ignored.
    note right of ELECTION_REQUESTED
        Coordinator considered crashed.
        ElectionTransaction requested.
        Further watchdog timeouts are ignored.
    end note

    %% Once ElectionTransaction starts, it owns the recovery process and this
    %% HeartbeatTransaction for the failed coordinator term has completed.
    %% [*] as a destination represents the end of its lifecycle.
    ELECTION_REQUESTED --> [*]: ElectionTransaction starts / heartbeat monitoring ends
